<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. da Vinci returns for his subsequent annual wellness visit. He completed the health risk assessment beforehand. His eyes cleared within a week. He wears the night elbow splint and the daytime anti-claw splint, goes to hand therapy twice a week, and has stopped leaning on his elbow at the drawing table. Numbness in the little finger is a little less; strength is about the same. He draws, writes, and teaches every day with his left hand, and has begun painting small panels with a palette fixed to the easel and built-up brush handles. He takes atorvastatin each evening without muscle aches. He has had no further falls; a handrail has been fitted on the open side of the stone staircase and lights added. He has had no emergency visits or hospital stays in the past year apart from today&apos;s care. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Subsequent annual wellness visit</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Ulnar neuropathy at the right elbow; hypercholesterolemia on atorvastatin</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Atorvastatin 20 mg</td></tr><tr><td>Safety events</td><td>One fall in the past year, the one that injured his elbow</td></tr><tr><td>Functional status</td><td>Independent in all activities and instrumental activities of daily living; buttons and jar lids still awkward</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Frustrated by his hand, but busy with drawing and students; no low mood</td></tr><tr><td>Behavioral</td><td>Never smoker; wine with meals, about seven glasses a week; walks an hour most days; plain diet with much fruit and vegetables</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr><tr><td>Instrumental activities of daily living</td><td>Independent; his household manages the shopping</td></tr><tr><td>Home safety</td><td>Handrail on both sides of the stairs and night lights added; smoke detectors working; no firearms</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Hears well; reading glasses; eyes recovered from the infection</td></tr><tr><td>Bladder</td><td>No leakage; mild nocturia once a night</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>No concerns</td></tr><tr><td>Pain</td><td>Occasional ache at the inner right elbow</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

